      "id": "kb_antiglycolic_session",
      "name": "KB Anti-Glycolytic Practice (Wildman)",
      "notes": "Anti-glycolytic KB session popularised by Pavel and taught by Wildman. Short timed sets (10\u201320 sec) of swings or snatches alternate with full rest until HR returns below ~130 bpm. Total session volume accumulates over 30\u201340 min; the glycolytic system is never taxed. Builds aerobic base and repeatable work capacity without accumulated fatigue or soreness. Breathing must remain nasal throughout \u2014 if mouth-breathing is required, the set was too long or the bell too heavy. This is not cardio: it is high-quality ballistic repetitions performed aerobically.\n",
